From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guido Urdaneta <guidou@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:53:34 -0800
Subject: [ImageCapture] Scope device session lookups to the requesting frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MediaStreamManager::VideoDeviceIdToSessionId() searched all active
device requests for a matching video device ID and returned the
session ID of the first match, regardless of which frame opened the
device. Since device IDs are per-origin rather than per-frame, two
frames using the same camera share a device ID but have distinct
sessions, so the lookup could resolve to a session that does not
belong to the caller.

Add a GlobalRenderFrameHostId parameter to VideoDeviceIdToSessionId()
and only consider requests made by that frame. ImageCaptureImpl now
passes the ID of its own RenderFrameHost when resolving the source ID
for GetPhotoState(), SetPhotoOptions() and TakePhoto(). If the frame
has no active session for the device, the lookup returns an empty
token and the request is answered with the default (empty) response,
as before.

Note that this means an ImageCapture object only resolves sessions
opened by the frame in which it was created; a frame holding a track
opened by a different frame (other than via track transfer) will get
empty results.

Add unit tests covering lookups from the owning frame, from other
frames, and from a second frame that opens the same camera.

Fixed: 579300424
Change-Id: I51b922f0134e45636dab47ebb4b2b146692222ff
